 "notes": "Old Dip pen kind became Dip pen holder; its nib, glass-pen and dip-pen models were split out: Brause 361/66 EF into Dip pen nib archetypes, J. Herbin and Wearingeul glass pens into Glass pen, Tachikawa T-25/T-40 and Speedball Standard holder into holder archetypes. New kinds Dip pen nib, Glass pen and Calligraphy fountain pen sourced from retrieved pages. Not added: Hario and Fuji glass pens (no page found); Sheaffer calligraphy sets (not on any retrieved page); Hunt 22B and Speedball nib dates beyond the A-series. Brause founding year and Japanese nib makers from knowledge; Nikko and Tachikawa founding years left blank. thepostmansknock and jetpens blocked; monk.ca and stlartsupply returned 404."
